# Prefer C++20

The repo builds with C++20 (`CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD 20`). New and edited code uses the C++20 standard library.

- Threads, mutexes, and condition variables are `std::jthread`, `std::thread`, `std::mutex`, and `std::condition_variable`.
- Do not include `pthread.h` or call `pthread_*` in new code.
- A platform API is acceptable only when C++20 has no equivalent. Naming a Windows thread for a crash dump uses `SetThreadDescription` for that reason. Other platforms leave the OS thread name unset.
- Do not rewrite existing platform thread code in an unrelated change.
